From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Thobe <fabian@thobe.eu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:02:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 182/182] PCI: make releasing BAR0 of Intel Arc integrated
 switches opt-in

Upstream has not settled whether the switch keeps decoding the address
range of the released BAR0. Until it has, only release it when booted
with pci_arc_release_bar0, and log a hint otherwise. Without the
parameter, the kernel behaves as before the quirk.
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt |  6 ++++++
 drivers/pci/quirks.c                            | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
index 03a55063064..3876b6bf197 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.txt
@@ -5324,6 +5324,12 @@ Kernel parameters
 				to disable PCIe TLP Processing Hints support
 				system-wide.
 
+	pci_arc_release_bar0[=<bool>]
+			[PCI] Release BAR0 of the PCIe switch integrated into
+			Intel Arc GPUs, so the BAR2 of the GPU can be resized to
+			cover its full VRAM even if the firmware does not
+			enable Resizable BAR. Off by default.
+
 	pcie_aspm=	[PCIE] Forcibly enable or ignore PCIe Active State Power
 			Management.
 		off	Don't touch ASPM configuration at all.  Leave any
diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index a147cb55fb0..4cec5cf11a2 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -6390,6 +6390,17 @@ DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_FINAL(PCI_VENDOR_ID_GLI, 0x9755, pci_mask_replay_timer_timeout
  * Release and disable BAR0 permanently by clearing its flags to prevent
  * anything from assigning it again.
  */
+static bool pci_arc_release_bar0_enabled __ro_after_init;
+
+static int __init pci_arc_release_bar0_setup(char *str)
+{
+	if (!str)
+		str = "1";
+
+	return kstrtobool(str, &pci_arc_release_bar0_enabled);
+}
+early_param("pci_arc_release_bar0", pci_arc_release_bar0_setup);
+
 static void pci_release_bar0(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 {
 	struct resource *res = pci_resource_n(pdev, 0);
@@ -6397,6 +6408,11 @@ static void pci_release_bar0(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 	if (!res->parent)
 		return;
 
+	if (!pci_arc_release_bar0_enabled) {
+		pci_info(pdev, "BAR 0 may prevent resizing the GPU BAR; boot with pci_arc_release_bar0 to release it\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (pci_release_resource(pdev, 0))
 		return;
 
